From 7103f07eb9bf53d898fae89cac69538d0911fc81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 13:37:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(scoring): sets/volleyball scorer UX fixes
 (MonoSetsLiveScore)

Addresses the multi-surface UX audit items in #108:

- Set-won notice: capture the COMPLETED set number into state at
  completion time (currentSet advances when the next set opens and
  never advances on the match-ending set, so reading it at render was
  wrong).
- Side-out serve switch now broadcasts: emit a value:0 point intent
  before the early return so spectators stay in lockstep; previously
  the switch wrote no backend event, so a later undo popped the last
  real point and desynced the watch.
- Loading vs not-found: track a load lifecycle and render the existing
  RouteRecoveryActions surface on not-found instead of a permanent
  "Loading...".
- Undo reverses serve in side-out: the serve switch records history
  (with the pre-switch servingTeam) and now broadcasts an undo in
  lockstep with the local restore.
- Per-team correction (-1): floor-at-0, history-recorded, never
  completes a set or rotates serve; mirrored as a value:-1 point.
- Deuce/serve rotation: gate the every-point-at-deuce switch to
  uncapped formats (!maxPoints) so it can never mis-fire for capped
  sports.
- Broadcast scorecardKind is now engine-derived (sets -> volleyball)
  rather than hardcoded.

Adds MonoSetsLiveScore.test.jsx (9 cases) covering set-won number,
serve-switch broadcast + undo, correction, not-found recovery,
rotation behavior, and engine-derived kind.

Closes #108

